From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 22:15:53 -0400
Subject: move the Space switcher to the bottom, as icons

A reference screenshot showed the switcher is a row of small icons at the
bottom of the sidebar, with the Space's name appearing on hover -- not a row of
named pills at the top, which is what the first version built. The pills also
made the sidebar top-heavy and pushed the tabs down.

Spaces gain an icon, which is what the switcher shows: the emoji the user picks,
on a chip in the Space's colour. The active Space's chip is full strength and
the rest are muted, so the row reads as one control with a selection. With no
icon chosen the coloured chip identifies the Space on its own.

Also drops the parked-tab tree from Space, and the class comments describing it.
That was the design ADR 0015 rejected -- it survived in the code as a second,
contradictory model of what a Space is. A Space owns no tabs; which tabs belong
to it is SpaceModel's business.

Why: the switcher was in the wrong place and the wrong shape, and Space had two
incompatible descriptions of itself.
Removable when: never, short of dropping Spaces.
